### 3. Summary of Findings

**KNIRVCONTROLLER** is a **React 19 + TypeScript** mobile/web application built with **Vite 6**, **Capacitor 8** (for native Android/iOS), and **Tailwind CSS**. It serves as the "Autonomous Gateway" mobile controller for the KNIRV decentralized network.

**Key architectural observations:**

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Framework** | React 19 + TypeScript 5.8 |
| **Bundler** | Vite 6.3 with `@vitejs/plugin-react` and `vite-plugin-node-polyfills` |
| **Mobile runtime** | Capacitor 8 (Android + iOS), configured in `capacitor.config.ts` (app ID `com.knirv.controller`) |
| **UI/Icons** | Tailwind CSS 3 + `lucide-react` icons |
| **Routing** | `react-router` v7 |
| **Wallet** | Local `knirvwallet-module` (from `core/packages/knirvwallet-module/`) |
| **Voice** | `@capgo/capacitor-speech-recognition` + `@capacitor-community/text-to-speech` |
| **QR scanning** | `capacitor-barcode-scanner` + `html5-qrcode` (fallback) |
| **PWA** | Service worker at `/sw.js`, web manifest, full PWA support |
| **Cloudflare** | Config via `wrangler.jsonc` with `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` |
| **Testing** | Vitest 4 + Testing Library + jsdom |
| **OCR/Schemas** | Hono 4.7 + Zod 3.24 on the backend |
| **Source entry** | `src/react-app/main.tsx` -> `App.tsx` -> 12 page components |
| **App structure** | 5-tab bottom nav (DVEs, Vault, Badges, Chat, Settings) with voice integration overlay |
| **Build/Release** | Custom scripts for PWA HTTPS preview, native mobile release, Android keystore signing, iOS manifest generation |

**Source directory breakdown:**
- `src/react-app/` -- Main React application (pages, components, hooks, platform adapters)
- `src/shared/` -- Shared types and cognitive-shell (EventEmitter, VoiceProcessor) shared across the app and worker
- `src/worker/` -- Cloudflare worker entry point (`index.ts`)
- `android/` -- Capacitor-generated Android native project
- `ios/` -- Capacitor-generated iOS native project
- `core/` -- Sub-monorepo containing `knirvwallet-module` (local wallet library)
- `public/` -- Static assets (favicon, PWA icons, brain.png, sw.js, manifest)
- `dist/` -- Production build output
- `build/` -- Release artifacts (signed APK, iOS manifest)
- `scripts/` -- Build/release automation scripts (ESM `.mjs`)

